**Standard error (standard deviation of the sampling distribution of the mean)**  

\[
SE = \frac{s}{\sqrt{n}}
    = \frac{1.4}{\sqrt{40}}
    = \frac{1.4}{6.3249}
    \approx 0.2214
\]

So the standard deviation of the null‑hypothesis test (i.e., the standard error of the sample mean under \(H_0\)) is **≈ 0.22**.
